=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 473
title: a weakened test whose callee calls the changed function from an unchanged module says production changed and was not its evidence
origin: #473 ruling Q4, new pin 2 (owner, 2026-10-18): #420's reproduction with `render` moved
origin2: into an unchanged module. The test calls `render`, which calls the changed `invoice_total`,
origin3: but the caller index reads only changed files, so no hop reaches it; #420's proposed fix
origin4: would not reach it either. The old label said no production change over a diff that
origin5: changed the very function the test runs.
=== head: views.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def render(items):
    return invoice_total(items, 0.05)
=== before: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)
=== after: billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax) + 5.0, 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from views import render


def test_invoice_renders():
    assert render([50.0, 50.0]) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from views import render


def test_invoice_renders():
    assert render([50.0, 50.0]) > 0
